<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy 28,000/T Aug N+A naphtha.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy 28,000/T Aug N+A naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy 28,000-tonnes of August naphthenic and aromatic (N+A) naphtha, a company official said on Friday.</p>
<p>CPC requires the cargo for August 1-31 delivery on a cost-and-freight (c+f) basis to Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>The tender closes June 25 and is valid for two days.</p>
<p>CPC's last tender, for July 20-31 delivery, was awarded at slightly above $215 per tonne c+f Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
